      "article_section": {
        "heading": "Uninstall CLI Plugins",
        "content": "<p>If you have created or installed a plugin using <a href=\"/docs/headless-cms/install-the-cli\">Contentstack CLI</a>, and want to uninstall/ remove that plugin, you can do it by using the <strong>plugins:uninstall </strong>command. </p>\n<p class=\"note\"><strong>Note</strong>: This command will not delete the plugin’s code folder. </p>\n<p>To do this, run the following commands in your terminal:<br></p><ol><li>Get a list of plugins you have installed:<br><pre>csdx plugins</pre></li><li><strong></strong>From the available plugins listed in the terminal, uninstall it by passing its name in the command below:<br><pre>csdx plugins:uninstall &lt;&lt;plugin_name&gt;&gt;</pre></li></ol>",
        "_metadata": {
          "uid": "csc5b4a1702fc77ced"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
